  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norec, FK Norway, personnell exchange</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CDP Trust and Zambian Women&apos;s Lobby are two grass root civil society organisations seeking to tap into each other&#x2019;s knowledge to enhance gender advocacy by addressing the issue of gender-based violence. Overall, they wish to include men as agents of change to prevent GBV in local communities in through their gender equality advocacy work.

ZNWL has an established programme for men and boys to strengthening their capacity and competence on addressing GBV in their local community. They seek to improve this programme by learning from CDP Trust&#x2019;s ArtasAdvocacy to provide more interactive and expressive art skills. CDP seek to expand men&#x2019;s involvement in their advocacy programmes regarding gender equality. ZNWL will share their competence on enabling young men to raise awareness among their peers and community about the negative effects of GBV.</narrative>
  </description>
